{"id":"h198","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"simpleqa","question":"How many concurrent FM synthesis channels (voices) can the Yamaha YM2203 from the 1980s handle? Is the answer \"3\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"The YM2203 (OPN) has 3 FM synthesis channels.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The datasheet and standard references list three FM channels, each with four operators.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The question asks specifically about FM channels, and the FM section has three channels.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The chip also has three SSG (AY-3-8910-compatible) square-wave/noise channels, giving six tone voices in total.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The SSG channels are PSG channels, not FM, so they should not count toward the answer.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"With four operators per channel the chip has 12 operators.","confidence":0.92,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Operators are not independent voices because they combine within a channel, so the operator count does not change the answer.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The answer 6 would be a mistaken answer to the FM channel question.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"su